      source: "Rijksmuseum, Amsterdam, object SK-A-581, 'Portrait of Hugo de Groot (1583-1645)', oil on panel, workshop of Michiel Jansz van Mierevelt, inscribed with his age 48 and the year 1631. The museum's own page says he posed for Van Miereveld during a short return to the Republic and that this panel is one of the many copies of that portrait, so it is a workshop copy of a portrait made from a sitting, not the original sitting itself and is recorded as a historical depiction. The painter died in 1641, so the panel is public domain by age; the Rijksmuseum page has an empty copyright field and Wikimedia Commons records the museum's statement that its images are public domain or CC0 (Commons file 'Portret van Hugo de Groot (1583-1645) Rijksmuseum SK-A-581.jpeg', original 4862 x 5680). The saved file was produced by downscaling a 1280 x 1495 Commons rendering of that original to 1027 x 1200; nothing was upscaled.",
